    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "# Wireframe Your Data Page\r\n\r\nIn this level, you’ll plan how your dataset will appear on the page.\r\n\r\n## Do This:\r\n\r\n1. Create a wireframe of your full page layout.\r\n   - Include a title/header.\r\n   - Include a short description area.\r\n   - Include a section where data cards will appear.\r\n   - Include placeholders for search, filter, or sort controls.\r\n\r\n2. Create a wireframe of one data card.\r\n   - Show where each data field will appear.\r\n   - Add clear labels or headings for the information users will see.\r\n\r\n3. Use arrows or notes to connect your schema fields to your card design.\r\n\r\nKeep your wireframes simple. Use boxes, labels, and arrows rather than detailed artwork.\r\n\r\nThis will guide how you build and render your dataset with `.map()` in the next level.",
